<title>ARGENTINA: Schroder Mildesa to launch open funds in Argentina.</title>
<headline>Schroder Mildesa to launch open funds in Argentina.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1996-08-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Schroder Mildesa Investment Management, joint venture of leading fund managers Schroders Plc and local  Banco Mildesa will announce Wednesday the launch of two new open-ended stock funds that will invest in Argentine and other Latin American shares.</p>
<p>Investment fund SMIM Equities will be launched August 29 and SMIM Latin America August 30, a spokeswoman for Schroder Mildesa told Reuters.</p>
<p>Schroders, the leading British fund managers, handles more than $110 billion in investments.</p>
<p>-- Guillermo Haskel, Buenos Aires Newsroom, 541 318-0650</p>
